From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:38:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dvc): bound per-channel and aggregate reassembly

Upstream's `DvcProcessor::max_message_size` (#2256) takes no limit unless a
processor sets one. A fragmented message is as long as its Data First PDU
declares, up to 4 GiB, and is held until it is complete; and a listener may
open a channel for every Create Request, each holding its own message.

The default is now 64 MiB (`DEFAULT_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE`); `None` still takes
messages of any length. The graphics pipeline takes up to 256 MiB (a frame
of uncompressed pixels for two 8K monitors side by side), display control
and audio input 1 MiB. On the client, the messages being reassembled on
all channels together may be at most as long as one message of the
channel that takes the longest: a fragmented message past that is refused
on its first fragment. Reassembly grows its buffer fallibly, up to the
declared size, and frees it when a message is dropped. The capture
replayer takes messages as long as the live channels do.
